Title:          microcodes-get-amd.tcz
Description:    get script to make early loading AMD microcodes
Version:        1
Author:         aus9 @ linuxquestions.org 
Original-site:  https://tinyurl.com/amdfirmware                
Copying-policy: open source
Size:           4.0K
Extension-by:   aus9 @ linuxquestions.org
Tags:           amd microcodes bios
Comments:       Based on my forum post 2023 in General TC Talk
                https://tinyurl.com/amdmicocodes but added an older microcode. 

                Its a get script and the resultant amd-ucode.img will be found at /tmp
                Loading the TCE will execute the script so please do NOT 
                have this in your boot list. Late loading microcodes are forbidden.               

                Before loading this TCE run $ dmesg | grep microcode
                and remember that value. Next load this TCE and copy that 
                amd-code.img to your boot Dir and adjust your grub.cfg at 
                the initrd line so it reads
                
                initrd /boot/amd-ucode.img (before your core or rootfs stuff)
 
                Full reboot and then recheck $ dmesg | grep microcode 
                to see if value changes. An updated bios should not have
                a changed value eg mine is unchanged 0x0a500014 

                An updated bios is better, but not all makers offer bios
                updates for older PCs. 

                Script has no idea if there a new updates so check  
                https://tinyurl.com/amdfirmware
                Forum post reply 2...discusses making a specific microcode script
                if interested.
      
